Aypa Power is a leading developer, owner, and operator of utility-scale energy storage and hybrid renewable projects that power our communities and cities. Our mission is to responsibly decarbonize the grid and make North American energy markets more affordable, sustainable, and efficient. Aypa is well-capitalized and uniquely positioned to lean forward on projects with well-suited deal structures to meet our customers’ needs. We have been at the forefront of energy storage development since our first energy storage project came online in 2018. As a leader in our industry, we have over 22 GW of utility-scale energy storage and hybrid renewable energy projects in development and 33 projects in operation or construction across North America.

The Director, Pre-Construction will play a critical role in the development and execution of Aypa’s portfolio of stand-alone battery storage and hybrid projects. This role will work closely with internal and external stakeholders to successfully plan, design, and prepare projects during the pre-construction phase.

Responsibilities:

• Lead, mentor, and develop a team of two (2) to three (3) direct reports, delegating workstreams effectively, setting clear priorities, and holding the team accountable for quality and deadlines;

• Develop and own integrated project execution schedules for utility-scale BESS and hybrid projects, identifying the critical path across engineering, major equipment lead times, permitting, interconnection, construction, and commissioning through COD; support the formation of project budgets;

• Collaborate with management to identify and review project risks, develop mitigation strategies, and ensure all potential issues are addressed proactively;

• Coordinate and contribute to engineering design reviews during late-stage development and provide input regarding feasibility and constructability;

• Lead the handover of projects from the Development Team to the Construction Team, including complete turnover packages, risk registers, and budget clarity;

• Oversee construction permitting strategy and submissions, including ministerial (by-right) permitting regimes, ensuring regulatory requirements are met and permit milestones are aligned with the execution schedule;

• Collaborate with the Engineering team to ensure project designs meet technical, vendor, and regulatory requirements and provide expert reviews on design documents, drawings, and specifications;

• Serve as the commercial lead for EPC contracting, from bid package and contractor selection through negotiation and execution, working with Legal, Finance, Engineering, and Procurement to negotiate key terms including contract price, schedule, liquidated damages, performance guarantees, warranties, credit support, and risk allocation;

• Prepare and compile EPC contract exhibits, including the scope of work, payment and milestone schedule, project schedule, technical specifications, and division-of-responsibility matrices;

• Support project financing and financial close by ensuring EPC contracts and exhibits are financeable under non-recourse structures and meet lender and tax equity requirements; support independent engineer and lender diligence and coordinate EPC-related conditions precedent to NTP;

• After NTP, support the Construction team in reviewing and validating EPC change orders under fixed-price contracts, challenging pricing, scope entitlement, and schedule impacts against the contract terms;

• Build and maintain strong, trusted relationships with EPC partners, balancing commercial rigor with a collaborative, long-term partnership approach;

• Coordinate interfaces between EPC contractors and BESS technology providers (e.g., Tesla, Sungrow, Fluence) to align supply agreements, EPC scope, delivery, and commissioning requirements;

• Work with Procurement to identify scope gaps before or after the execution of respective contracts;

• Lead and administer meetings with EPC contractors, suppliers, and interconnecting utilities for projects before mobilization;

• Maintain effective communication with internal project teams, contractors, and external stakeholders, ensuring all parties are informed and aligned;

• Ensure that projects adhere to environmental and safety standards and assist in the development of safety plans and protocols;

• Own pre-construction document control, creating, organizing, and maintaining contracts, exhibits, permits, and reports in line with Aypa’s processes and systems, and prepare regular progress reports for senior management and stakeholders;

• Adopt and implement Aypa’s pre-construction processes, templates, and standards across the team and portfolio;

• Other duties as assigned or required.

Key Qualifications:

• Bachelor's degree in engineering, project or construction management, environmental science, or a related field;

• Eight (8) or more years of experience in utility-scale renewable energy, with significant time in EPC commercial, pre-construction, or project management roles; experience working for an EPC contractor is strongly preferred;

• Utility-scale BESS experience is strongly preferred; solar and/or wind experience will also be considered;

• Demonstrated experience negotiating EPC contract terms and drafting and compiling EPC exhibits, including the scope of work, payment schedule, and technical specifications;

• Working knowledge of non-recourse project finance and the IPP financing process (construction and term debt, tax equity, independent engineer review, and conditions precedent), and how EPC terms affect financeability;

• Experience reviewing change orders and challenging EPC pricing under fixed-price (lump-sum) contracts;

• Clear understanding of project execution schedules, critical path management, and BESS commissioning processes through COD;

• Experience with major BESS technology providers (e.g., Tesla, Sungrow, Fluence) is highly desirable;

• Experience leading and delegating to a team, with a track record of developing direct reports;

• Proven ability to build and sustain collaborative relationships with EPC partners while protecting the owner’s commercial interests;

• Highly organized, with strong document control and document creation skills, and a willingness to adopt and implement Aypa’s established processes;

• Professional Engineer (P. Eng, PE) and/or Project Management Professional (PMP) designations considered an asset;

• Proven track record of taking utility-scale projects from late-stage development through EPC execution, financial close, and NTP;

• Strong working knowledge of Primavera P6 and/or MS Project;

• Strong technical, analytical, and problem-solving skills;

• Excellent communication, negotiation, and teamwork abilities;

• Proficiency in project management software and tools (Procore);

• Clear understanding of energy-sector permitting, including ministerial (by-right) permitting regimes.

Compensation and Location:

Salary: Full-time base salary commensurate with experience.
Bonus: An annual bonus will be awarded based on both individual performance as well as the overall success of the business.
Benefits: Aypa offers an attractive benefits package with excellent health care/dental/vision, 401k matching, unlimited vacation, paid parental leave, and other health/wellness benefits.
Location: Hybrid (USA). Ability to work in the United States is a requirement. Preference is given to candidates located in Austin, TX, or willing to relocate. Remote will be considered on a case-by-case basis.

At Aypa, we nurture and support a highly diverse team and actively seek to advance fair and inclusive practices in all aspects of what we do. We hire passionate, dedicated, and forward-thinking individuals from different backgrounds and value unique perspectives and experiences. With a focus on belonging, we are committed to providing an inclusive environment for all.

